dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot (1.0-4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Documentation now derives from an org-mode source of truth at build time:
    checkpassword-dovecot(8) and dsmr-smtpauth(8) man pages, plus a
    dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot info manual and HTML page covering the bridge's
    theory of operation, the auth-client wire protocol, configuration, and
    debugging hints.  Generators (pandoc, emacs, texinfo) are Build-Depends
    only; the production host gains no new runtime dependency.

 -- Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>  Fri, 05 Jun 2026 09:00:00 -0400

dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot (1.0-3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dsmr-smtpauth: populate uid/gid/home/shell from getent passwd when the
    user is a Unix account, so /etc/dovecot/system-passwd doubles as the
    userdb for IMAP/Maildir access.  Entries of the form user:hash:::: are
    sufficient for SMTP AUTH but break dovecot 2.4 IMAP because mail_path
    (~/Maildir, set by 99-vpopmail-mail.conf) requires the userdb to return
    a home directory.  Non-Unix users continue to get the minimal hash-only
    entry — they remain authorized for SMTP relay with no Maildir access.
  * dsmr-smtpauth passwd: preserve uid/gid/home/shell from the existing
    record (or refresh from getent passwd) instead of overwriting them.

 -- Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>  Tue, 12 May 2026 16:45:00 -0400

dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot (1.0-2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add dsmr-smtpauth(8) admin tool for managing /etc/dovecot/system-passwd.
    Subcommands: add, del, list, passwd, test.  Atomic edits under flock,
    SHA512-CRYPT hashing via doveadm pw with the password fed on stdin
    (never the command line).  The 'add' subcommand auto-verifies the
    new credential by running the bridge end-to-end against dovecot.

 -- Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>  Sun, 10 May 2026 16:30:00 -0400

dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot (1.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Bridges qmail-smtpd checkpassword-program protocol to dovecot's
    auth-client over a Unix socket, letting qmail submission share
    dovecot's chained passdb stack (vpopmail SQL, /etc/dovecot/system-passwd,
    PAM) for SMTP-AUTH.
  * Ships /etc/dovecot/conf.d/99-dsmr-smtp-auth.conf, an auth-client
    listener readable by vpopmail:vchkpw.
  * Reloads dovecot and cycles qmail-submission on configure.

 -- Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>  Sun, 10 May 2026 11:00:00 -0400
